    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Hello, I’m Guangtan!” This friendly "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "greeting",
            "ref": "v-greeting"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " comes from a French chef. In his online videos, he speaks Chinese and cooks with great "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "passion",
            "ref": "v-passion"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". With his hands, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "home-style dishes",
            "ref": "v-home-style-dish"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " turn into wonderful meals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, “Chef Guangtan” has over six million fans on Chinese social media. He even calls himself “a French chef with a Chinese stomach”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Guangtan grew up in a small city in northern France. When he was seven, he tried Chinese food for the first time and fell in love with it. Years later, he came to Beijing as a student. He enjoyed his classes, but his favourite lessons came outside the classroom—through food. He learned to cook Chinese food from a kind cleaning lady in his "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "dormitory",
            "ref": "v-dormitory"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". In the following four years, Guangtan travelled across China as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "backpacker"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". He ate his way through every city he visited."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In 2010, during the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Shanghai World Expo",
            "zh": "上海世博会"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Guangtan came back to China. There, he began mixing Chinese and Western dishes in new ways. Since then, Shanghai has become his home."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Soon, he started posting his cooking videos online. At first, Guangtan felt a little nervous. “I was worried that people might say, ‘How can a foreigner cook Chinese food?’” he said. But to his surprise, he soon got many fans and they loved his videos very much. “I’ve learned so much from the comments,” the man said with a smile."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Guangtan has now lived in China for 18 years. He is married to a Chinese woman, and they enjoy their life in Shanghai. “Food is a wonderful way for East and West to understand each other,” he said. “Don’t be afraid to taste something new. Who knows? You might find a new favourite dish and learn about a new culture, just like I did!”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
